From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] f_output_chain: wake the chain after a hard reset

mp_output_chain_reset_harder() resets the chain's filters but never wakes
the chain itself. A request from downstream can stay pending, and the
reset chain then sits idle until some unrelated wakeup arrives.

The hard reset runs on every reload of the audio output (the ao-reload
command, an output's own reload request such as the AVFoundation output's
fallback from passthrough to PCM, and audio option changes that reload the
output), on the spdif-to-PCM fallback in reinit_audio_filters_and_output()
and on video's hardware decoding fallback.

At the end of the hard reset, after the existing reset work, call
mp_filter_wakeup() on the chain's own filter. Applies to mpv v0.41.0.

